    {
      "id": 17225,
      "name": "Chaosmancer",
      "username": "Chaosmancer",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/chaosmancer/{size}/1977_2.png",
      "created_at": "2017-09-30T20:55:16.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So, I normally don't post about mechanical things and such, but I just had a match with Xtreme Fanatic for the first time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I randomized in the Video Game and got Plague Rat, and then I added in Legacy because I got an evil idea.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>First turn, Infection was played on Fanatic. Every turn thereafter, I used \"Kill the Spirit\" and all my infection damage (with legacy boosting and the last turn with a Explosives Wagon from Silver Gulch) was redirected to Plague Rat. It was sooooo much fun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, for the first time in... I think ever? I played Chastise. I've pretty much never played that card, because taking the damage isn't generally worth it and there are very few targets I want to just delay instead of trying to destroy, but with this version? It was just a delayed damaging one shot, and also kept the locus around longer (cause why not have more +1's when trying to burn down the rat)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I really, really, like this version of Fanatic</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:50:13.602Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 9,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
