      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>So, I normally don&#39;t post about mechanical things and such, but I just had a match with Xtreme Fanatic for the first time.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I randomized in the Video Game and got Plague Rat, and then I added in Legacy because I got an evil idea.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>First turn, Infection was played on Fanatic. Every turn thereafter, I used &quot;Kill the Spirit&quot; and all my infection damage (with legacy boosting and the last turn with a Explosives Wagon from Silver Gulch) was redirected to Plague Rat. It was sooooo much fun.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Also, for the first time in... I think ever? I played Chastise. I&#39;ve pretty much never played that card, because taking the damage isn&#39;t generally worth it and there are very few targets I want to just delay instead of trying to destroy, but with this version? It was just a delayed damaging one shot, and also kept the locus around longer (cause why not have more +1&#39;s when trying to burn down the rat)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>I really, really, like this version of Fanatic</p>",
